// Negative control for `assume_sum_positive` (design/wildcards [20] gap 1).
//
// The wildcard is inhaled only under `b`, so the merged total is genuinely `0` on
// the `!b` path and the read must NOT frame. This is the shape the fix has to
// refuse, and it refuses it structurally rather than by a side condition: where
// two chunks' presence guards differ, `merge_chunks` folds each guard into its own
// amount as `guard ? p : 0`, and `perm_known_positive` requires EVERY leaf of a
// summand to be positive — the `0` arm is not. So a conditionally-present wildcard
// states nothing here, which is the truth.
//
// Positive counterpart: `tests/cases/passing/permissions/wildcard_sum_positivity.vpr`.

field f: Int

method gated_wildcard_does_not_frame(x: Ref, b: Bool)
{
  if (b) {
    inhale acc(x.f, wildcard)
  }
  var v: Int := x.f
}
